==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}}, from Old French, from the Old Italian ''cavalcata'' from ''cavalcare'', which meant to ride on horseback, from Medieval Latin ''caballicāre'', from the {{etyl|la}} ''[[caballus]]'', which means [[horse]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkævəlˌkeɪd/|/ˌkævəlˈkeɪd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-cavalcade.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|eɪd}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[company]] of [[rider]]s.
# A [[parade]].
# A [[trail ride]], usually more than one day long

====Synonyms====
* {{italbrac|company of riders}}: [[company]]
* {{italbrac|parade}}: [[parade]], [[procession]]

